      "inputTokens": 136,
      "outputTokens": 1043,
      "costUsd": 0.009455,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's a bigger model. A new theme park has sixty-two thousand visitors in its first year, and three thousand five hundred more each year after that. Its visitors in year n are sixty-two thousand, plus n minus one increases, because the first year has no increase yet. That simplifies to three thousand five hundred n, plus fifty-eight thousand five hundred. Over the first ten years, the total is S ten. That's five, times one hundred and twenty-four thousand, plus nine increases. So it's five times one hundred and fifty-five thousand five hundred, which is seven hundred and seventy-seven thousand five hundred visitors."
