      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 96,
      "outputTokens": 791,
      "costUsd": 0.007167000000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "In which year do its visitors first go over one hundred thousand? Set the formula above one hundred thousand. Then three thousand five hundred n is more than forty-one thousand five hundred, so n is more than about eleven point eight six. Years are whole numbers, so it's year twelve. Check both sides. Year eleven has ninety-seven thousand visitors, and year twelve has one hundred thousand five hundred. Notice that year twelve comes after eleven increases, not twelve."
