      "costUsd": 0.0105985,
      "pronunciationText": "Watch the wording about time. A young tree is one hundred and twenty centimetres tall when it's planted, and it grows forty-five centimetres each year. How tall is it after six years? Here the starting height is at time zero, before any year has passed. After one year, there's one year of growth. After six years, there are six. So the height is one hundred and twenty, plus six lots of forty-five, which is three hundred and ninety centimetres. As a sequence that starts at the planting height, that's the seventh term, not the sixth. So when the first value is in year one, year n has had n minus one changes. When the start is time zero, after n years means n changes."
