      "pronunciationText": "Day n comes after n minus one drops, so the pile holds one hundred and eighty, minus four lots of n minus one. Set that below one hundred. Then n minus one is more than twenty, so n is more than twenty-one. The first day below is day twenty-two, with ninety-six logs. Day twenty-one is wrong. On that day the pile holds exactly one hundred, not fewer."
